      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, if the typeface was nullptr originally then this bit won\u0027t be set so you\u0027ll currently end up with a font with nullptr for typeface. Of course if you then try to read the typeface but it doesn\u0027t deserialize then you\u0027ll still get nullptr back from the read, so that\u0027s not something to assert about, that\u0027s just normal (tried to deserialize an skp and didn\u0027t know how to deserialize it). That\u0027s just an unflattening error. (Not sure if we want to recover or not, but shouldn\u0027t crash.)",
      "revId": "07d15a0950623fb93e2eed684c6b60ac33b63e41",
